         "A small Jewish farming village (about 200–400 people) in a sheltered basin at 350–400 m, away from the main roads. Not mentioned in the Hebrew Bible, Josephus or the Mishnah — hence Nathanael’s question: “Can anything good come out of Nazareth?” (John 1:46). Excavations: cisterns, silos, hiding tunnels and dwelling caves of the 1st c. After the Temple’s destruction the priestly course “Hapitzetz” settled here.",
