         "According to the Protoevangelium of James (2nd c.), Mary first heard the angel’s voice while drawing water at the spring. The church, built in Dahir al-Umar’s time, stands over Nazareth’s ancient spring. A carved, gilded wooden iconostasis; steps lead down to a vaulted Crusader chapel where the water rises from a stone well.",
